 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfE-88jjAuy/",
 "title": "How to End a Speech Without Saying Thank You",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator explains why ending a presentation with 'Thank you' is a waste of the final 30 seconds. Instead, he shares a three-step framework to finish with impact using a core message, a clear call to action, and a memorable final line.",
 "key_points": [
  "Never waste the last 30 seconds of a presentation by saying 'Thank you' and 'that's everything for today.'",
  "Step 1: Remind the audience of your one big message. Remember that confidence comes because you speak, not before you speak.",
  "Step 2: Tell the audience what you want them to do next. For example, invite someone to speak this week when they normally would stay quiet.",
  "Step 3: Finish with one short, memorable line they will remember.",
  "Treat your voice like an instrument and learn how to play it."
 ],
 "content": "Never End a Speech With “Thank You” This is the perfect example on how to end a speech. [Speaker in video clip]: P.S. follow your dreams, not your boyfriend's. I've trained leaders at companies like Google, Visa, and Asics, and most people completely waste the last 30 seconds of their presentation. They say, so yeah, I think that's everything for today. Thank you. Don't do this. Instead, use these three steps. First, remind them of your one big message. So remember, confidence doesn't come before you speak, it comes because you speak. Second, tell them what you want them to do next. This week I invite you to speak once when you normally would stay quiet. And third, finish with one short line they'll remember. Your voice is an instrument, learn how to play it. Recap, action, and memorable line. Try this and follow for more simple tips to become a magnetic speaker.",
